@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
    ViewData["MetaDescription"] =
        "Meet Comfy Capy Calories, a friendly calorie and nutrition tracker for easier food logging.";
    ViewData["CanonicalUrl"] = "https://calories.comfycapy.com/About";
    ViewData["Robots"] = "index,follow";
}

<div class="content-page">
    <p class="page-eyebrow">About the app</p>
    <h1>Nutrition tracking, made a little comfier</h1>
    <p class="lead">
        Comfy Capy Calories is a calorie and nutrition tracker built to make food logging feel
        useful and easy to use, without all the faff.
    </p>

    <div class="content-card">
        <h2>What you can do</h2>
        <p>
            Set a personal calorie target, search USDA FoodData Central, create your own foods and portions,
            and keep a daily Diary with calorie and macronutrient totals. Historical Diary entries preserve
            the nutrition information you logged at the time.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-card">
        <h2>Why the Capy?</h2>
        <p>
            Tracking nutrition can be tedious or intimidating. The Capy isn't. He is comfy. We want to 
            make your experience here comfy too.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-card">
        <h2>Our design philosophy</h2>
        <p>
            Nutrition tracking can be a real pain in the capy. It can feel like another chore to tack onto 
            your life. Instead, we try to make things accessible, easy to understand, and dare I say a little
            fun. So grab a chair and get settled, and make something that truly feels like your own.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="alert alert-info" role="note">
        Calorie targets and nutrition values are estimates for general information and tracking, not medical advice.
        Read the fuller <a asp-page="/Help" asp-fragment="nutrition-estimates">nutrition guidance</a> before relying on them for health decisions.
    </div>
</div>
